+# MASTER7 customer withdrawal requests
+
+Updated: 2026-11-05 MYT
+
+## Delivered flow
+
+1. An approved customer opens **Withdraw**.
+2. The customer selects one of four separately recorded companies: VPay, GSPAY, 1MPAY or GSPAY+.
+3. The customer selects a Malaysian bank and enters account-holder name, account number and an MYR amount.
+4. The portal checks the available wallet amount, reserves the requested amount and creates one pending request.
+5. The MASTER7 owner backoffice shows an immediate pending-request notice and the full request details.
+6. The owner processes the request in the selected company's backoffice and updates MASTER7 through Approved, Processing, Paid or Rejected.
+7. Rejected requests release the reserved amount. Paid requests reduce the member wallet once.
+
+This release does not automatically submit a payout to a payment provider. That matches the owner's latest instruction: MASTER7 receives the request first, and the operator then processes it in the selected provider backoffice.
+
+## Data protection
+
+Bank account holder and account number are encrypted at rest with the server-only `WITHDRAWAL_DATA_KEY`. Customer history only returns the last four digits. Exports omit encrypted fields. The key is not included in source, reports or browser code.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Four independent provider choices and 18 Malaysian banks.
+- Member-only, approved-account access with existing origin and CSRF controls.
+- Available-balance and one-open-request checks.
+- Owner-only full details and valid status transitions.
+- Wallet hold, rejection release and paid deduction tests.
+- Complete local suite: 87 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped.
+- JavaScript syntax and Render production build passed.
